{% call note("info", "Good to know", "Different labels answer different questions") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Keep Mbps and milliseconds separate. A result about throughput is not the same as a result about responsiveness. Do not use a single score as a guarantee about every website, call or room.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="section-4"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Decide what to ask next</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Write: “Using [test] on [device], in [room], at [time], I recorded [label, value and units]. The problem I was investigating was [symptom].” An unexplained result is a useful question for the provider or technician; it is not proof that you need new hardware.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-coverage-or-internet-service/">coverage worksheet</a> for location comparisons or <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-dropout-diary/">dropout diary</a> for intermittent trouble. The <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-dropouts-diagnosis/">Wi-Fi pillar</a> covers the wider diagnostic picture.</p>


